# Datasets and outputs — NEVER commit (guarded by .claude/hooks/guard-bash.sh).
# Every path here is leading-slash anchored to the repo root. Unanchored, `data/` matches ANY
# directory named `data` at any depth — which is how `src/gdp/data/` (spec 01's entire deliverable)
# ended up excluded from both git and ruff, and uncommitted. `/data/*` rather than `/data/` so git
# still descends into the directory: an excluded *directory* is never traversed, which would make
# the grounding-eval re-inclusions at the bottom of this file silently dead.
/data/*
/runs/
/checkpoints/
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
/wandb/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
venv/
env/
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.sublime-project
.sublime-workspace

# Credentials & secrets
secrets.json
credentials.json
.aws/
*.pem
*.key

.claude/

# macOS
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
*.DS_Store

# Miscellaneous
.cache/
*.log
*.log.*
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Allow test fixtures (tiny, synthetic, must be committed)
!tests/fixtures/**

# Spec 04's grounding eval set is the ONE thing under data/ that must be committed. H9 permits a
# self-built benchmark only because "its construction, bias, and drop-rate are fully documented",
# and design decision 6's hash-freeze is only auditable if the reviewer can see both the phrases
# and the lock. All three are small, hand-authored text. The overlays (rendered JPEGs) and
# frames.json stay ignored — they are regenerable from `gdp ground sample-frames --seed`.
!/data/grounding_eval/
/data/grounding_eval/*
!/data/grounding_eval/construction.md
!/data/grounding_eval/phrases.json
!/data/grounding_eval/phrases.lock.json
CLAUDE.md
specs/
grounded-driving-perception-spec.md
progress_report.md
MANUAL_TESTING.md
